## Why do we backtrack?

Suppose

```text
      1
     / \
    2   3
```

After finishing the left subtree,

the prefix sums from that path **must not** be used while exploring the right subtree.

Therefore,

after returning from recursion,

remove the current prefix sum.

```java
map.put(currentSum, map.get(currentSum) - 1);
```

This keeps the map valid for the current root-to-node path only.

